---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Deliberately selected, published writing. These links ship in the HTML even
// when the sibling site is unavailable during a build. Use its clean URLs.
const writing = [
  {
    title: 'How I use AI',
    href: 'https://probablyfine.dev/blog/how-i-use-ai',
    description: "I use these tools a lot. This is where I've landed on what that should mean for the work I put out.",
  },
  {
    title: 'I built dnsweaver because I was tired of managing DNS by hand',
    href: 'https://probablyfine.dev/blog/why-i-built-dnsweaver',
    description: 'Every new service needed a DNS record. I wanted to stop doing that by hand.',
  },
  {
    title: 'I just wanted to play games',
    href: 'https://probablyfine.dev/blog/i-just-wanted-to-play-games',
    description: 'My mom got me into DOS games. Wanting to play more of them eventually got me into working on computers.',
  },
];
---

<Layout>
  <section class="portfolio-intro page-shell" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Solutions &amp; Infrastructure Architect</p>
      <h1 id="intro-title">How Far Can We Take This?</h1>
      <p class="intro-copy">I design enterprise infrastructure and make the case for building it. I also look after what happens once it's running. Today that means owning an Azure platform that thousands of devices depend on across four global regions.</p>
      <p class="intro-proof"><strong>38% fewer platform support tickets</strong> year over year, measured in the customer's ServiceNow.</p>
      <div class="intro-links">
        <a href="/resume" data-track="cta-resume" class="primary-link">Read my resume <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href="/about">More about me <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="intro-aside" aria-labelledby="outside-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Outside Work</p>
      <h2 id="outside-title">Server Legos</h2>
      <p>I wanted a way to watch movies. Somehow that turned into a Kubernetes cluster and a house full of things I host myself. I'll still turn down a night of gaming if there's a project in the lab I'm excited about.</p>
      <a href="https://probablyfine.dev/blog?utm_source=maxfieldallison&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=portfolio" data-umami-event="outbound-probablyfine">Visit probablyfine.dev <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="work-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2 id="work-title">Selected Work</h2>
    </div>
    <article class="work-example">
      <p class="eyebrow">Enterprise Architecture</p>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="/projects/test-environment" data-track="case-study-test-environment">Before It Hits Production</a></h3>
        <p>Every change went straight to production. Getting a test environment approved took five months, from finding the right team to making the case for the money. I designed the environment, and the platform teams own the provisioning.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="work-example">
      <p class="eyebrow">Open Source</p>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="/projects/dnsweaver" data-track="case-study-dnsweaver">DNS That Keeps Up</a></h3>
        <p>I'd remove a service and forget its DNS record. After enough of that, I wanted a tool that would clean up after it. That's dnsweaver. I own the design and releases, with AI agents writing the code.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="work-example">
      <p class="eyebrow">Upstream Contribution</p>
      <div>
        <h3><a href="/projects/opnsense-frr" data-track="case-study-opnsense-frr">The Issue a Bot Closed</a></h3>
        <p>The BGP setting I needed wasn't exposed in the interface. An issue asking for it sat unresolved until a bot closed it. I picked it up, and the change shipped upstream.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
    <p class="section-more"><a href="/projects">All case studies <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="portfolio-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <h2 id="writing-title">Beyond the Case Studies</h2>
      <p>I've been writing more at probablyfine.dev, about the things I'm working on and how I got into all of this in the first place.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="writing-list">
      {writing.map((post) => (
        <li>
          <h3><a href={`${post.href}?utm_source=maxfieldallison&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=selected-writing`} data-umami-event="outbound-probablyfine">{post.title} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3>
          <p>{post.description}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>
</Layout>
